{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434063-beshilu-articles","id":1434063,"title":"Beshilu Articles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-31T17:48:35-08:00","id":1434063,"title":"Beshilu Articles","content":"So we have some real active beshilu in our game that are gnawing holes in the border between Hisil and Earth and killing people to take command and spread their influence. What would be some articles you might see in the proper news channels from this increased activity? Murders with hearts removed, etc.? What about some posts that Network Zero might have put up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T20:15:25-08:00","id":1434076,"title":"","content":"I think you'd see some weird pieces similar to the 2020 stories about rats attacking people. In real life it was due to them having less to scavenge because of less people going out. There was also a story about <a href=\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2020/10/29/new-york-city-sidewalk-collapses-rats/6078036002/\" target=\"_blank\">someone who was walking on the sidewalk and it collapsed beneath them, and they ended up in a hole full of rats</a>. So, if the beshilu were active (in rat form) in certain places you might get public health warnings, and increased restaurant fines or shutdowns due to the increased number of the vermin.<br /> <br /> Since they tend to get host bodies to do a lot of their more relevant activity they might work on trying to get some relevant bodies, like reporters or health officials, to deny that there's really problems.<br /> <br /> You might get an increase in YouTube or other social media videos about rats acting weird, like pizza rat or the viral 'rat taking a shower' one. They would be easy to dismiss due to the easy access to digital alteration software people have but folks like PCs in the know could see them as evidence, especially if they know areas from the videos are now rents in the Gauntlet. You'd also have other things coming in, like disease spirits, which doesn't bode well for anyone. The fiction in the second edition core book touches upon the effects of a full-scale beshilu assault on a city and the place is basically quarantined due to all the outbreaks.<br /> <br /> I think for Network Zero you'd probably not want to jump instantly to 'last scions of a species of progenitor god-entities that once stalked the earth' and probably lean heavy on the 'superintelligent rats' thing, getting videos or witness statements about rats acting in strangely intelligent ways, maybe sightings of rats that seemed to talk to people (actually beshilu in human forms). It could be easy to find a scapegoat for this sort of thing. From there it can evolve to, or parallel, the sort of 'so-and-so has been replaced!' body-snatcher type story, from people who notice physical deformities on the human beshilu, as they slowly turn more rat-like.<br /> <br /> Since once the beshilu have human hosts they're going to start eating folks you're going to have increased missing persons reports (or not, if they're quiet about it) maybe human traffickers of different sorts get caught without seeming to be trafficking people (because they were eaten), fringe groups on the outskirts of town disappearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T22:40:14-08:00","id":1434088,"title":"","content":"Also, clickbait-looking headlines that turn out not to be clickbait. I'm thinking specifically of that Chipolte in NYC that got shut down recently, where so many of the online news articles went with dramatic phrasing like &quot;Rats Have Taken Over This Restaurant.&quot; We're so used to that kind of crazy exaggeration that it doesn't always register, but when your characters click through they'll find out, actually, that's pretty accurate...<br /> <br /> There might not be much direct news coverage if the human hosts they're targeting are already on the social margins, but the news would report if a local church or other org started making a fuss after multiple unhoused people/day laborers/recovering addicts go missing. Same if a community group started complaining about rats in the neighborhood - individual incidents might not make headlines, but activists might raise a stink in the media if they want to put pressure on landlords/local government. This doubles as giving your players some NPCs to go talk to (and giving the Beshilu someone to target for calling attention to their schemes).<br /> <br /> One thing I have Network Zero doing in my Demon game is picking apart audio/video evidence to authenticate it - going frame by frame, identifying evidence of tampering or interference, trying to replicate a particular effect with mundane means to prove that what they've got <i>isn't </i>mundane. Is this a monster, or is it a combination of poor lighting and a weird angle making [x] seem like a monster? Is this evidence of deliberate image tampering or just an artifact of the hardware/the file compression/the camera settings? That sort of thing. Might be a nice tension breaker to see a thread start with a clear, unambiguous video of a rat-hybrid, followed by several people debating whether that's make-up and one person trying to replicate it with forced perspective and a hamster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T08:16:03-08:00","id":1435642,"title":"","content":"I think that things would generally start getting much weirder. If the gauntlet is thin than I imagine it would be easy for spirits to cross over and start urging and claiming people. There would be articles of people behaving in extreme ways depending on which type of spirit urged them. This can run the gamut from &quot;man eats 256 hotdogs&quot; to people who start cults of personality. This is usually when the Storm Lords start getting very busy.<br /> <br /> BTW, once the Beshilu start rending the gauntlet, is there a way to fix it or is it permanently broken?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}